values ('c1d2e3f4-5a6b-4c36-9f56-6d7e8f9a0b96', 'introduction-to-the-new-testament', 'Introduction to the New Testament', 'Introduce the New Testament as a collection of ancient texts studied historically, literarily, religiously, and ethically. Students learn how the collection was transmitted and canonized, place Jesus, Paul, and early communities in Jewish and Greco-Roman contexts, read the Gospels, Acts, letters, and Revelation with critical methods, and practice exegesis, reception history, material and digital study, and responsible interpretation in a research capstone.');

