oncept", "title": "Social-scientific criticism"}], "description": "Critical methods give students tools for asking evidence-based questions about ancient texts."}, {"id": "cee374c2-b914-4371-ac28-14488d248846", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reading ancient texts responsibly", "children": [{"id": "e019a396-86bc-48d4-b5f2-f3fa4954ed73", "type": "concept", "title": "Ancient context"}, {"id": "40c4bb70-0c15-4fb3-8894-28eb3ecb4a93", "type": "concept", "title": "Genre awareness"}, {"id": "6c597421-d9cc-491f-b359-bdb1e7000507", "type": "concept", "title": "Anachronism"}, {"id": "da78e6e9-a6d3-41a2-b414-58377800be31", "type": "concept", "title": "Reader positionality"}], "description": "Responsible interpretation requires attention to context, genre, translation, and reader assumptions."}]}, {"id": "5897fb8f-37bd-45ae-a113-8a52a6db777d", "type": "topic", "title": "Texts, Canon, Translation, and Manuscripts", "description": "Learn what the New Testament is, how it was transmitted, and how translations and canons shape reading.", "children": [{"id": "8a33ca8a-d090-4c98-960a-2ffb619878c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What is the New Testament", "children": [{"id": "70839033-f46a-400a-9923-bf6fb6a622d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Gospels"}, {"id": "ac4c49d4-6ad8-4768-8e17-f3299c7508d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Acts"}, {"id": "b0010518-1416-4d22-ac8f-f38fc7f3f6e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Letters"}, {"id": "397b4b64-5222-417b-9cb2-9763c427641d", "type": "concept", "title": "Apocalypse"}], "description": "The New Testament is a library of writings, not one book written at one time."}, {"id": "fc1e8365-3777-402c-80b7-bae127432db2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Canon and collections", "children": [{"id": "35dac5ba-6634-4add-8f42-352e2d478830", "type": "concept", "title": "Fourfold Gospel"}, {"id": "7e14cc31-eaa5-467c-9746-c0f4e366d056", "type": "concept", "title": "Pauline corpus"}, {"id": "d044a5c9-d031-4303-a80e-c4ee5715163a", "type": "concept", "title": "Catholic epistles"}, {"id": "ef03e3c7-fcbb-4f42-8d0b-b73ac69c8643", "type": "concept", "title": "Canonical lists"}], "description": "Canon formation explains how communities recognized, used, debated, and bounded authoritative writings."}, {"id": "76d0af89-4b39-4755-b653-2dc7382d6edb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Translation and manuscripts", "children": [{"id": "e0f0e8e5-628b-4da9-864e-ebdd543b67f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Greek manuscripts"}, {"id": "04e111ca-95a8-47ee-b5e3-457aeaa33d31", "type": "concept", "title": "Modern translations"}, {"id": "e4064a94-96f6-4af7-adb2-67730312095e", "type": "concept", "title": "Textual variants"}, {"id": "d35c65cd-37ed-4942-bda6-fe44bcfd4d37", "type": "concept", "title": "Study Bible notes"}], "description": "Translation and manuscript variation remind students that every modern Bible is an interpreted edition of ancient evidence."}]}, {"id": "b1cf7812-2ae5-4f96-ae37-289dcb95cb16", "type": "topic", "title": "Second Temple Judaism and the Greco-Roman World", "description": "Place Jesus, Paul, and early Christian communities within Jewish, Hellenistic, and Roman contexts.", "children": [{"id": "7490d12c-07d6-496c-b1cf-8df17a207fc8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Second Temple Jewish context", "children": [{"id": "083fba03-e10c-4c68-bbf2-eed63e7841ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Temple and priesthood"}, {"id": "b0c859ac-4d62-4205-b59c-9967a1282306", "type": "concept", "title": "Pharisees and Sadducees"}, {"id": "afb18dd7-1d67-4d3f-a079-315cf7ae3519", "type": "concept", "title": "Apocalyptic hope"}, {"id": "5d617521-7823-4da7-9dfc-f4a9e49d7cec", "type": "concept", "title": "Dead Sea Scrolls"}], "description": "Jesus and the first Christians were part of Jewish worlds shaped by scripture, temple, law, sectarian debate, and empire."}, {"id": "97cc2b67-6338-4cbd-96f5-b1fee3909308", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Greco-Roman context", "children": [{"id": "22eb1c15-2e51-4a17-806b-e162188c5b57", "type": "concept", "title": "Roman rule"}